@participant3 
Regarding the ability to resize a transparent window by dragging its borders, as I mentioned earlier, from a code perspective, Electron has never officially supported this. On Windows, when transparent: true is set, Electron internally removes the `WS_THICKFRAME` window style and sets `thick_frame_` to false. See https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/winmsg/window-styles for reference.

Relevant code snippet. 
```c++
// shell/browser/native_window_views.cc
...
if (transparent())
    thick_frame_ = false;
...
// We should not show a frame for transparent window.
if (!thick_frame_) {
  frame_style &= ~(WS_THICKFRAME | WS_CAPTION);
...
// thickFrame also works for normal window.
if (!thick_frame_)
   FlipWindowStyle(GetAcceleratedWidget(), false, WS_THICKFRAME);

```

